<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siege of Baghdad (1258)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1258</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Mongol destruction of Baghdad, Mongol invasion of 1258, Mongol sack of Baghdad, sack of Baghdad</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> in 1258 was the capture and sack of the Abbasid capital by the Mongol army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hulagu-khan">Hulagu</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-mustasim">al-Musta'sim</a> was executed and much of the city's population killed. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a> profile treats the event as the end of the caliphate in Baghdad, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a> profile notes its impact on the region.</p></div>
